WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.530
At boundary points outside
Makkah, pilgrims stop,

2
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:06.530
make an intention, and
change their clothes.

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.300
Men put on two plain
white unstitched cloths.

4
00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:14.190
Perfume, cutting hair and
quarrelling are now forbidden.

5
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.370
For centuries the journey
took months, by land and sea.

6
00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.400
Then came the aeroplane.

7
00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:23.240
Why do pilgrims dress so simply and alike,

8
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.830
and what changed when they began to fly?

9
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.910
In this mission, you'll
follow the rites day by day,

10
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:32.360
from seven circuits of the
Ka'bah to stoning the pillars.

11
00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:35.640
Then you'll see what air travel
changed in the last century,

12
00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:37.270
and what it did not.

13
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.820
Your mission: find out what
the pilgrim's clothing means,

14
00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:43.310
and how modern travel reshaped Hajj.
